    {
      "id": "p0175-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In standard written Japanese, most characters share the same size and adhere to a grid format. In computer lingo, these are sometimes referred to as \"full-width characters\".",
        "raw": "In standard written Japanese, most characters share the same size and\nadhere to a grid format. In computer lingo, these are sometimes referred\nto as \"full-width characters\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12270742,
          0.11245714,
          0.67670269,
          0.15736429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.12066587,
          0.11174286,
          0.67874424,
          0.15843571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在规范的日文书写中，大多数字符大小相同，排列成整齐的方格。用计算机术语来说，这些字符有时叫作“全角字符”。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
