    {
      "id": "p0175-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "For various technical and historical reasons, early Japanese computing systems used \"half-width characters\". These squished characters allowed two characters to fit in the space of one standard character. This came at a cost, however: the half-width character set only supports one Japanese writing system: katakana.",
        "raw": "For various technical and historical reasons, early Japanese computing\nsystems used \"half-width characters\". These squished characters allowed\ntwo characters to fit in the space of one standard character. This came at\na cost, however: the half-width character set only supports one Japanese\nwriting system: katakana.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12318719,
          0.17057857,
          0.67549817,
          0.25042857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
